<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Khaniadhana State</h1><p class="st-meta">1724 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Khaniadhana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Bundela Rajput principality in Bundelkhand, an offshoot of the ruling house of Orchha.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Khaniadhana was founded in the early 18th century by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela Rajputs</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/orchha-state">Orchha</a>, one of several small holdings created as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundela</a> kingdoms divided among heirs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded of its internal history. Under British paramountcy it was a minor state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand-agency">Bundelkhand Agency</a>, ruled by a Raja over a few dozen villages, without a gun salute.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Khaniadhana acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> after 1947 and was absorbed in 1948. Its former territory lies in Shivpuri district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/khaniadhana-state.jpg" alt="Khaniadhana State" width="320" height="196"><figcaption>Image: Great Britain India Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Datia-Samthar_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1724 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Khaniadhana</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Khaniadhana</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1836&amp;focus=khaniadhana-state" aria-label="Khaniadhana State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6754 1257 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Khaniadhana State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7074 1513L7364 1601M7074 1513L7364 1602M7074 1513L7064 1471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7064 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7074 1513h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7074 1513h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1836&amp;focus=khaniadhana-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
